# The dangling else. X -> else S | epsilon.
#   FIRST(else S) = {else}
#   FOLLOW(X)     = {else, $}   (because S X sits inside  S -> if b then S X)
# The token 'else' is in BOTH predict sets -> a nullable/FOLLOW conflict.
# Not LL(1) as written; real parsers resolve it by always taking  X -> else S
# (else binds to the nearest if).
%start S
S -> if b then S X | other
X -> else S | epsilon
